1
00:00:03,659 --> 00:00:10,199
Start on the Home screen. The Architecture
template sets one unit to 30 cm.

2
00:00:10,249 --> 00:00:17,669
Grid and walls follow it: walls
one unit thick and nine units high.

3
00:00:17,719 --> 00:00:23,939
Ok, lay the floor. On the Civil
tab, choose Rectangular Slab.

4
00:00:23,989 --> 00:00:31,106
Click two grid points: nine metres by six.

5
00:00:31,156 --> 00:00:37,536
Now the walls. The Wall tool draws a connected chain.

6
00:00:37,586 --> 00:00:51,656
Snap to each corner of the
floor. Walls join by themselves.

7
00:00:53,265 --> 00:00:56,686
Press Enter to finish the chain.

8
00:00:56,736 --> 00:01:10,205
Openings need points up the wall, so
place axis helpers along its base.

9
00:01:10,255 --> 00:01:19,061
Add Hole: click up one helper on the
wall, then the base of the other.

10
00:01:19,111 --> 00:01:28,605
Same again for the window, on its own two helpers.

11
00:01:28,655 --> 00:01:34,555
Good. The helpers have done their
job, so Clear Guides removes them.

12
00:01:34,605 --> 00:01:41,385
Holes are only openings. Doors
and windows are separate objects.

13
00:01:41,435 --> 00:01:47,893
Door: snap to two opposite corners of the opening.

14
00:01:47,943 --> 00:01:57,530
Ooh, nice. Now the same with the Window tool.

15
00:01:57,580 --> 00:02:07,505
Finish with a roof: one more slab,
snapped to the top corners of the walls.

16
00:02:07,555 --> 00:02:13,216
Niiiice! Right-drag to look around the finished cabin.

17
00:02:13,266 --> 00:02:21,186
Everything stays editable: select
a wall later to change its height.
